From e7322e95e8ff523444fbab70d08f8d0b07c0584e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@tuta.io>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 13:20:29 +0800
Subject: media: i2c: s5kjn1: Apply exposure and analogue gain together

Applications can supply exposure and analogue gain in one V4L2 control
request. Cluster the two controls and write them under the sensor's
group hold so they do not latch separately. The Xiaomi Pad 8 Pro's
OS4.0.6.0 S5KJN1 FillExposureSettings sequence uses the same 0x0104
hold and release writes.

Always attempt to release the hold, including after a failed data
write. When a shorter frame needs an exposure adjustment, use the
same cluster and leave the old exposure range on error. If the
adjustment succeeds but the frame length write fails, keep the shorter
exposure and the old range. Do not attempt to undo a sensor write
whose completion is unknown.

Exercise clustered and single controls, controls cached while stopped,
CCI error handling, and frame length retry with the ARM64 V4L2 core and
a test register bus.

Assisted-by: LLM

Require reinitialization before accepting live updates after a failed sensor register transaction.
